BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Write to the Mic Dodge Poetry Teen Workshops
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T190000
UID:db45c1109fdb76b1c3b17ee4a6bb1292@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Everyone’s voice is different. We want to hear&nbsp\; yours 
 . This winter/spring\, come together with other teens (ages 13 to 18) from
  across Newark at a &nbsp\;Dodge Poetry workshop &nbsp\;designed to showca
 se your words and ideas. Poets from the community ( like &nbsp\; Newark’
 s first-ever poet laureate\, Mia X )\, and students from the&nbsp\; Rutger
 s-Newark MFA program in Poetry \, will be on hand to offer prompts\, sugge
 stions and ideas. But the focus is on you: &nbsp\;What frustrates you? Whe
 re do you find joy? What does this city and this country look like from yo
 ur unique\, powerful perspective? We believe poetry can be found in books\
 , but also in hip hop\, at protests and parties\, in the clip of a song pl
 aying from the window of a passing car.&nbsp\; Poetry is an oral tradition
  \, especially here in Newark. (Even our&nbsp\; mayor&nbsp\; is a spoken w
 ord artist\; this is what we do!) So be a part of the conversation. Join u
 s to write your own verses\, and then (if you choose) speak them out loud 
 at the&nbsp\; open mic that ends every session . Workshops are FREE &nbsp\
 ;and will be held in person on the first Wednesday of the month (at locati
 ons in various wards in Newark\; see below for details) and virtually on t
 he third Wednesday of the month. THEME: Youth Poetry Workshop (Ages 13-18)
  / Open Mic HOST: NJPAC FEATURES: Poets from the community ( like &nbsp\; 
 Newark’s first-ever poet laureate\, Mia X )\, and students from the&nbsp
 \; Rutgers-Newark MFA program in Poetry \, will be on hand to offer prompt
 s\, suggestions and ideas. PRICE: FREE RSVP - https://www.njpac.org/event/
 write-to-the-mic-dodge-poetry-teen-workshops/#rsvp CONTACT: IG - @njpac / 
 FB - NJPAC
LOCATION:Clinton Hill Community Action - Zion Hill Baptist Church\, 152 Os
 borne Terrace\, Newark\, NJ\, 07112
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/write-to-the-mic-dodge-poetry-
 teen-workshops-8-5
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LetItFlow Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T220000
UID:432c629eac375b814a4f2f195179e288@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Name of Event: Let It Flow at the House of Playokee Date: Aug 
 5\, 2026 Start/End Time: 6:30 pm Address: 1050 Stuyvesant Ave\, Union\, NJ
  Theme: Open Mic and features Host: Elijah Brown Feature(s): P.O.M.E * JSK
 ILLZ * POETRESS * PARADISE * SOULETIC Price: $20 Advance Tickets / $25 At 
 Door - CashApp - $Elijahbr85 / Venmo - @Elijahbr1985 / PAYPAL @ElijahBr0wn
  Phone: TEXT (862) 306-1758 Email Address: &nbsp\; lifpublishing@gmail.com
  Website: Social Media: &nbsp\; @elijahbr85 Event Description: &nbsp\;&nbs
 p\;Support doesn’t always mean buying a ticket. As I prepare to celebrat
 e 21 years of hosting the Let It Flow Poetry Series\, I know everyone won
 ’t be able to attend\, and that’s okay. There are still so many ways y
 ou can help make this celebration special. You can: Purchase a ticket. Sha
 re or repost the flyer. Tag someone who loves live entertainment. Sponsor 
 a ticket for someone who may not be able to afford to attend. Leave a comm
 ent about your Let It Flow experience if you’ve ever been to one of our 
 shows. If you’ve never experienced Let It Flow\, this is the perfect tim
 e. It’s more than poetry. It’s laughter\, storytelling\, live performa
 nces\, community\, and moments that stay with you long after the show ends
 . Whether you’re planning a girls’ night out\, a date night\, or just 
 looking for something different\, you’ll leave with something to talk ab
 out. And I’ll make you this promise… If you come to the show and hones
 tly don’t enjoy yourself\, I’ll personally refund your ticket. That’
 s how much I believe in what we’ve built over the last 21 years. Thank y
 ou to everyone who’s supported this journey. Whether you’re in the roo
 m\, sharing the event\, or cheering from afar\, you’ve been part of this
  legacy. Come Let It Flow.
LOCATION:House of Playokee\, 1050 Stuyvesant Ave\, Union NJ\, Union\, NJ
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/letitflow-open-mic-aug-3
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
