BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GRILLS &amp\; GRIOTS
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260808T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260808T160000
UID:2c58b32858d1b7bb1fea00965975d144@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:#block-yui_3_17_2_1_1783631740960_25715 .sqs-gallery-block-gri
 d .sqs-gallery-design-grid { margin-right: -20px\; } #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1
 783631740960_25715 .sqs-gallery-block-grid .sqs-gallery-design-grid-slide 
 .margin-wrapper { margin-right: 20px\; margin-bottom: 20px\; } GRILLS &amp
 \; GRIOTS &nbsp\; Something special is coming to Willingboro! Join us for 
 the inaugural&nbsp\; Grills &amp\; Griots \, a new annual poetry series pr
 esented by&nbsp\; NJ Poetry Events &nbsp\; @njpoetryevents in partnership 
 with&nbsp\; Mocha Mic with Millie . &nbsp\; Saturday\, August 8 &nbsp\; 1:
 00 PM – 4:00 PM &nbsp\; Willingboro Lakes Park 60 Beverly-Rancocas Rd. W
 illingboro\, NJ 08046 We will be coming together under the&nbsp\; gazebo &
 nbsp\;for an afternoon of delicious barbecue\, dynamic spoken word perform
 ances\, meaningful conversation\, and a welcoming community gathering cele
 brating the power of poetry. &nbsp\; Hosted by: &nbsp\; Millicent Ansah &n
 bsp\;( @millicent_ansah24 ) Poet\, curator\, educator\, and founder of&nbs
 p\; Mocha Mic with Millie&nbsp\; ( @mochamicwithmillie ) &nbsp\; Grill Mas
 ter: &nbsp\; James C. Ellerbe &nbsp\;( @james.c.ellerbe ) Spoken word arti
 st\, author\, and founder and administrator of&nbsp\; NJPoetryEvents.com &
 nbsp\; ( @njpoetryevents ) &nbsp\; Featuring &nbsp\; AVG &nbsp\;( @avgpoet
 ry ) Poet\, author\, and activist whose work explores faith\, identity\, r
 omance\, and social justice\, inviting audiences into spaces of reflection
  and healing. &nbsp\; Sincerely L.&nbsp\; ( @poeticaptitude_ ) Nationally 
 ranked slam poet and author of&nbsp\; Sunflower Soldier \, whose poetry em
 braces honesty\, healing\, vulnerability\, and transformation. &nbsp\; Ope
 n Mic &nbsp\; 10 open mic spots available! &nbsp\;Whether you're a seasone
 d performer or stepping up to the mic for the first time\, we'd love to he
 ar your voice. &nbsp\; Admission:&nbsp\;$25 for Adults &nbsp\;(14 years an
 d up) -&nbsp\; $12 for Kids &nbsp\;(5-13 years) -&nbsp\; Free &nbsp\;(Unde
 r 5 years) - Purchse tickets below . &nbsp\;Registration includes your cho
 ice of a barbecue meal selected during checkout. &nbsp\; Plant-based meal 
 options are available. &nbsp\; No walk-ins. &nbsp\;Advance registration is
  required. &nbsp\; This is an alcohol-free event. &nbsp\; Behind the lens:
  &nbsp\;Expressions by MowZus will be capturing the memories\, the moments
 \, and the magic of the day through photography. &nbsp\; What is Grills &a
 mp\; Griots? Inspired by the rich storytelling tradition of griots\,&nbsp\
 ; Grills &amp\; Griots &nbsp\;is a new annual gathering that blends poetry
 \, food\, and fellowship to create a safe and welcoming space where Black 
 poetic voices are celebrated\, stories are shared\, and community is stren
 gthened. &nbsp\;Everyone is welcome to attend. &nbsp\; This is a family-fr
 iendly event! &nbsp\;Bring the kids\, invite your friends\, and enjoy an a
 fternoon of great food\, inspiring poetry\, and community in the park. Com
 e hungry. Come inspired. Come ready to connect. &nbsp\;We'll bring the gri
 ll. &nbsp\;You bring the poetry. &nbsp\;Together\, we'll build community\,
  one poem and one plate at a time. PURCHASE TICKETS #block-yui_3_17_2_1_17
